      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vik,' Here 'Vika' sets up the idea, while 'Vika' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Походу, сработал твой план.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Looks like your plan worked.' A compact expression built around 'apparently' and 'plan'. And Vika jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Замолчи, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Shut up, please.' Notice the word order: 'to fall silent' comes first, and 'to fall silent' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Это наш новый хозяин.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
